				<r3d:description language="eng">The Crustal Dynamics Data Information System (CDDIS) was initially developed to provide a central data bank for NASA&#039;s Crustal Dynamics Project (CDP). The Crustal Dynamics Data Information System (CDDIS) supports data archiving and distribution activities for the space geodesy and geodynamics community. The main objectives of the system are to store space geodesy and geodynamics related data products in a central data bank, to maintain information about the archival of these data, and to disseminate these data and information in a timely manner to NASA investigators and cooperating institutions.</r3d:description>
